  "worked_solution": "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=\u27e81+5t,1+2t,1-4t\u27e9.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=\u27e81+5t,1+2t,1-4t\u27e9$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot \u27e82,-3,5\u27e9 & =36 \\\\ \u27e81+5t,1+2t,1-4t\u27e9\\cdot \u27e82,-3,5\u27e9 & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =\u27e81+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8-9,-3,9\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$",
